  "details": "Over the several hours in VRChat Official Pride Hub Music Event, (bot) users without an active VRC+ subscription or gifts (such as [MapleAI](https://vrchat.com/home/user/usr_187b11fa-f71d-4166-bbfe-a49091559894) and [Celeste-AI](https://vrchat.com/home/user/usr_ff803344-a3a9-4949-b7a6-900b9b7b0b22)) seemed to receive an disproportionate amount of VRC+ gifts over the course of the event compared to the rest of the event population. The bots had no active VRC+ at the time the bot accounts joined the instance, and those accounts staid for several hours in the instance. | OPERATOR | reportedly said Celeste-AI received 8 months of VRC+ during the event (out of ~100 gifts, in an instance with 80 concurrent users).\n\nVRC+ gift drops default to an option of prioritizing gifting VRC+ for those without an active VRC+ subscription.\n\nThis could be RNG / bias in my observation. There may be a bug where the VRC+ subscription status is not updated within an instance after a non-VRC+ user receives a VRC+ gift, making that user count as a non-VRC+ user (or bot) for gifting as long as the user/bot stays within the instance and gifts keep dropping.",
